# core/view-usage-semantic - Which diagrams show this element, without the views graph?
#
# Answers: the same question core/view-usage answers, from the other of the two
# statements converter output makes about view membership. Reads the one-hop
# arch:inView edge on the element itself, in the SEMANTIC graph, instead of finding
# a node in the views graph that points at it.
#
# Does NOT prove: that an element absent from every diagram is unimportant, nor that
# appearing on many makes it central. Diagram membership is an editorial choice.
#
# WHEN TO USE THIS RATHER THAN core/view-usage. Prefer core/view-usage where the
# views graph exists — it is the richer route and it names the node, so it can tell
# two drawings of one element apart. This one exists for the case that route cannot
# serve: a graph published with `--views-profile no-views` or `no-diagrams` has no
# views graph, so core/view-usage returns zero rows and an undrawn element is
# indistinguishable from one whose evidence was dropped at publication.
#
# Requires roles.in_view, so it is refused against output converted before core
# 0.4.0. The two templates cover different datasets; the profile decides.
#
# RETURNS NO ?node COLUMN, unlike core/view-usage. There is no node on this route.
# A caller reading that column must use core/view-usage, and a caller counting rows
# should know these differ where an element is drawn twice on one view: this reports
# the view once, core/view-usage reports each node.
#
# Unlike its counterpart this needs no cross-graph join. core/view-usage reaches into
# views for the node and back into semantic for the view's own label and viewpoint;
# here everything is semantic, so the view's label and viewpoint sit beside the edge.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT DISTINCT ?view ?viewLabel ?viewpoint
WHERE {
  {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
    VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
    ?focus {{ROLE:in_view}} ?view .
    OPTIONAL { ?view {{PATH:label}} ?viewLabel }
    OPTIONAL { ?view {{ROLE:conforms_to_viewpoint}} ?viewpoint }
  {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
}
ORDER BY ?viewLabel ?view
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
